WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:02.690
Simple features beat most
AI control monitors.

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:03.650
Here's the setup.

3
00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:05.990
An AI agent slips
two lines into a file.

4
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:07.656
A monitor reads the problem
and the code,

5
00:00:07.716 --> 00:00:09.520
and scores how suspicious it looks.

6
00:00:10.316 --> 00:00:11.437
Score every solution,

7
00:00:11.497 --> 00:00:14.866
and a good monitor pulls the honest
and backdoored piles apart.

8
00:00:15.116 --> 00:00:18.126
These are 24 published monitors,
from best to worst.

9
00:00:18.216 --> 00:00:20.516
Now add a word counter
that never runs the code.

10
00:00:20.576 --> 00:00:21.946
It beats 20 of them.

11
00:00:23.115 --> 00:00:24.225
Why does that work?

12
00:00:24.475 --> 00:00:26.565
Each pile was written
by a different author.

13
00:00:26.635 --> 00:00:29.595
People write compact code,
and models add spaces.

14
00:00:29.655 --> 00:00:32.445
And 1 in 7 test backdoors
can never even trigger.

15
00:00:32.803 --> 00:00:36.023
Keep the problems but swap the authors,
and the score follows them.

16
00:00:36.083 --> 00:00:39.533
With backdoors by Claude Sonnet 5,
it rises to 0.95.

17
00:00:39.623 --> 00:00:42.513
When Sonnet 5 writes both sides,
it drops to 0.75.

18
00:00:42.974 --> 00:00:45.180
So we rebuilt the benchmark
with one author,

19
00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.584
and checked that every backdoor works.

20
00:00:47.774 --> 00:00:51.714
A Sonnet 5 monitor catches 77%
of the older models' backdoors.

21
00:00:51.774 --> 00:00:54.634
Of its own,
it catches only 37%.

22
00:00:54.694 --> 00:00:56.826
Count only the ones that work,
and that rises to 61%.

23
00:00:56.886 --> 00:00:57.904
Still fewer.

24
00:00:58.463 --> 00:01:00.418
So before you trust
a monitor benchmark,

25
00:01:00.478 --> 00:01:02.475
report baselines
that never run the code,

26
00:01:02.535 --> 00:01:04.665
pair each class with code
by another author,

27
00:01:04.725 --> 00:01:06.913
and check that every backdoor works.

28
00:01:07.183 --> 00:01:09.585
Because a high score on a benchmark
is not, by itself,

29
00:01:09.645 --> 00:01:11.513
evidence of sabotage detection.

